{
  "id": "eog",
  "term": "EOG",
  "definition": "EOG, or electrooculography, is a biological test that measures the eye’s resting electrical signal between the cornea and retina while the eyes move a fixed amount in dark- and light-adapted conditions. How much this signal rises in light is used to check the health of the retinal pigment epithelium.",
